# image-tools Python backend dependencies — the GOVERNED, RANGED inputs.
#
# This is the source-of-intent for the per-scenario isolated venv. It is compiled
# (uv pip compile --generate-hashes) into requirements.lock, which is the fully
# pinned + hashed version SSOT that the venv is actually synced from. Edit ranges
# HERE, then regenerate the lock (see internal/pydeps/README.md) — never edit
# requirements.lock by hand.
#
# App-compatibility CEILINGS live here (not in the shared SDA governance ranges):
#   transformers <5 — diffusers 0.38 loads SD/InstructPix2Pix checkpoints through
#   the transformers 4.x CLIP layout (CLIPTextModel.text_model), which 5.x removed.
#   >=4.49 keeps Qwen2.5-VL support (Qwen-Image-Edit-2509). The SDA governance
#   range (>=4.41) carries only the security/license posture.
#
# SCOPE: the proven, runnable Python backends only —
#   * diffusers generative/edit stack: instruct-pix2pix, qwen-image-edit,
#     sd-1.5-inpainting (edit_instruct / inpaint / outpaint / background_replace),
#     plus the conditioning/adapter layer (LoRA / ControlNet / IP-Adapter) which
#     loads adapter weights through diffusers' PEFT backend (peft);
#   * ONNX Runtime inference stack: denoise/deblur/segment/detect/tagging/
#     embedding/colorize and the other CPU-floor onnx ops.
# The basicsr/facexlib RestoreFormer++ face-restore path is intentionally EXCLUDED:
# its execution adapter is gated (sidecar restore.py refuses to run pending the
# restoration golden path), and its old basicsr/facexlib stack would pin torch/
# torchvision down for the whole env. It is added — and proven — when that vertical
# lands, not before.

